<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE gslv-f18-nvs03 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — GSLV-F18 / NVS-03 (IRNSS-1L), SDSC-SHAR Second Launch Pad — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 4.83 s, kick 8.179 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.742, payload 2250 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.3919--0.000072*(t-t_ign stage 2).
Vehicle config: GSLV Mk II (S139+4 L40H+GL40HT+CUS15) (sim/vehicles/gslv_mk2.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
GSLV Mk II TIMELINE mode: stage/fairing event times are ISRO&#x27;s PUBLISHED GSLV-F15/NVS-02 sequence (same vehicle, same 2,250 kg NVS GTO class); ISRO has not published an F18 event table.
Stage loads and masses from the ISRO GSLV-F18/NVS-03 brochure (27 Oct 2026); thrust/Isp from Wikipedia (GSLV, Vikas, CE-7.5, PSLV) with derivations noted.
Not flown: LL2 NET 2026-10-30T18:21:00Z (Fri Oct 30 11:21 am PDT; 23:51 IST), window 17:00-21:00Z, status Go (LL2 updated 2026-10-28T08:54Z). Spaceflight Now&#x27;s schedule does not list it.
Hazard areas: NAVAREA VIII 1127/26 (rocket launching 301700-302100Z Oct; zones 2-4 centroids bear 106.1/106.3/106.7 deg from the pad at 601/1017/1768 km) and NOTAM A3241/26 (VOMF, 30 Oct-11 Nov 1700-2100Z).
EVENT TIMES ARE THE GSLV-F15/NVS-02 PUBLISHED SEQUENCE (ANALOG): ISRO&#x27;s F18 brochure (27 Oct 2026) gives orbit, masses and azimuth but no event table.
Target (see launch config): insertion 302 km, apoapsis 37023 km, fpa 7.453 deg, launch azimuth 105.75 deg; payload 2250 kg.
Pad: 13.719900N 80.230400E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-10-30T18:21:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF note: No post-cutoff burns: GSLV CUS15 is single-burn; the spent CUS stays in the ~170 x 37,000 km GTO (debris).
Post-cutoff / two-rev coast WITHHELD: fitted insertion is suborbital (perigee ~-5 km vs F18 target 170 km); altitude residuals vs F15 analog knots are 22-60 km low. PR left open pending retune.
Deploy time unpublished (F18 brochure has no event table); F15 analog S/C sep was T+1150.38 s.</description>
